# Environment variables for the portfolio (Vite SPA + Vercel serverless API)
# Vite only exposes variables prefixed with VITE_ to the CLIENT at build time.
# The contact-form secrets below are SERVER-side (no VITE_ prefix) and are never
# shipped to the browser — they are read by api/contact.js (Vercel) and by the
# Vite dev middleware (vite.config.js) when running locally.

# ── Contact form backend (Nodemailer → Gmail SMTP) ─────────────────────────
# Copy these into a local `.env.local` file (gitignored) for local dev, and add
# the same values under Vercel → Project → Settings → Environment Variables for
# production. The form POSTs JSON { name, email, message } to /api/contact.
# EMAIL_USER=your.sender@gmail.com
# EMAIL_PASS=your_gmail_app_password   # Gmail App Password, NOT your password
# EMAIL_TO=your.inbox@gmail.com        # optional; defaults to EMAIL_USER

# NOTE: Never commit real secrets. `.env*` files are gitignored except this example.
